17. In two recent decisions of the Supreme Court;
Leach and Co., Ltd. v. Jardine Skinner
and Co., (5) and Pirgouda Hongunda Patil v. Kalgunda Shidgunda Patil, (S) their Lordships have laid down that all amendments ought to be allowed which satisfy the two conditions namely (a) of not working injustice to the other side, and (b) of being necessary for the purpose of determining the real questions in controversy between the parties. Their Lordships observed was even in a case where a fresh suit on the amended claim would be barred by limitation on the date of the application for amendment, the Court would allow the amendment if that is required in the interests of justice.
